---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# Reverts a `Stream.map` that never fused — the analogue of 441 and 442 for the
# plainest operator of all. 306 folds every `Φ.hone.map` into a distill in the
# hope that a neighbour joins it; when its neighbours are barriers (a capturing
# filter, a `limit`, a `sorted`, a terminal), the distill leaves the fuse pass
# still carrying nothing but the one call to the mapper 202 took from the
# lambda, and 501/511 would lower it into a `mapMulti` over a fresh
# `distill_N` method. One operation becomes one operation, and the stage now
# costs a wrapper call and a sink it did not have before (#1128).
#
# The shape matched here is exactly what 306 leaves when nothing fused: a
# stateless, static `map` distill whose body is the single `invokestatic` of a
# `lambda$…` method and no more (closed body, no 𝐵-rest). A distill that found
# a neighbour carries the neighbour's opcodes too, a non-static one has had
# 311's `this` load spliced in, and a map whose ends 421/422 re-typed has an
# unwrapping on its body, so none of those can match. `accepted` and
# `returned` must equal the bridge types: that is how 202 minted them for a
# plain object lambda, and it is what makes the bridge signature rebuilt below
# the very one javac emitted.
#
# ORDER MATTERS: it runs after 401 (every object operator has collapsed into
# one distill), after 411/421/422 (the ends are aligned) and after 451 (a
# trailing mapToX has had its chance to fuse into the same distill). By 453
# nothing else will be added to the body, so a body of one is a map that
# stayed alone.
#
# What goes back is the `Φ.hone.lambda` 202 consumed, as 452 does, so 701
# lowers it to the original `invokedynamic` + `Stream.map` and 711/712 strip
# the wrapper a desugared method reference left behind. The lambda carries the
# `reverted ↦ Φ.true` marker: 202's pattern is closed on the ten bindings 111
# mints, so the eleventh stops it recognising this map a second time and the
# 202 -> 306 -> 453 cycle cannot spin on a run with more than one cycle.
name: unfused-map-to-lambda
pattern: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.distill,
    class ↦ 𝑒-class,
    bridge-input ↦ 𝑒-bridge-input,
    bridge-output ↦ 𝑒-bridge-output,
    start ↦ "map",
    accepted ↦ 𝑒-accepted,
    returned ↦ 𝑒-returned,
    static ↦ "true",
    state ↦ ⟦⟧,
    body ↦ ⟦
      𝜏-call ↦ ⟦
        φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokestatic,
        i2 ↦ 𝑒-target-class,
        i3 ↦ 𝑒-target-method,
        i4 ↦ 𝑒-target-signature,
        i5 ↦ 𝑒-target-is-interface
      ⟧
    ⟧
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.lambda,
    class ↦ 𝑒-class,
    method ↦ "apply",
    interface ↦ "()Ljava/util/function/Function;",
    lambda-signature ↦ "(Ljava/lang/Object;)Ljava/lang/Object;",
    bridge-signature ↦ 𝑒-bridge-signature,
    static ↦ "true",
    opcode ↦ "invokestatic",
    target ↦ ⟦
      handle ↦ 6,
      class ↦ 𝑒-target-class,
      method ↦ 𝑒-target-method,
      signature ↦ 𝑒-target-signature,
      is-interface ↦ 𝑒-target-is-interface
    ⟧,
    stream ↦ ⟦
      class ↦ "java/util/stream/Stream",
      method ↦ "map",
      signature ↦ "(Ljava/util/function/Function;)Ljava/util/stream/Stream;"
    ⟧,
    reverted ↦ Φ.true
  ⟧
when:
  and:
    - matches: ['lambda\$.+', 𝑒-target-method]
    - eq: [𝑒-accepted, 𝑒-bridge-input]
    - eq: [𝑒-returned, 𝑒-bridge-output]
    - matches: ['^(L.+;|\[.+)$', 𝑒-bridge-input]
    - matches: ['^(L.+;|\[.+)$', 𝑒-bridge-output]
where:
  - meta: 𝑒-bridge-signature
    function: concat
    args: ['"("', 𝑒-bridge-input, '")"', 𝑒-bridge-output]
